module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: MechanicallyPreventable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the convergence planner and the lib.rs renderer both derive crate-root membership from the partition the run itself declares, so a PR that adds a seed module converges in one heal invocation with no generated file installed by hand beyond the module's FIRST mirror, whose install is a deliberate authorial act rather than a gap: the host refuses to admit an emitted-but-uncommitted surface because an authored module and an emitter that invented a surface produce the same population (required_regen_host.rs:1562-1576)",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "SPECIMEN (NAMESPACE-XL wave 1, PR #14317, 2026-10-18): the wave made std.host_text a dependency of seed-mirrored modules (std.coercion, gunbc.rust_crate_package_ident, extdeps.version.semver), so a new stage0 module std_host_text entered the seed. After the partition row and the produced mirror were committed, heal-generated-artifacts (`claim_executor --regen-round-cost`) still refused, printing only `convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant Refused`. Exposing the planner's payload (a local, unpushed edit of v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_stage_plan_kind_label) read: SeedMembershipUnresolved { reason: lib.rs has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition, surface: RegenSurfaceIdentity { declaring_module: v1.compiler.emit_rust, projected_path: lib.rs } }. The lib.rs the candidate tree held was itself TRANSITIONAL: committing it got past the planner, but once the regenerated partition mirror was installed too, the candidate lib.rs no longer declared std_host_text (a partition crate owns it) and lib.rs returned to main's bytes -- so the planner refused twice on two different lib.rs states before either was the fixed point.",
    "WHAT ONE NEW SEED MODULE COST, IN ORDER, each a separate heal round and each a generator output installed outside the job that owns it: (1) the partition row (v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition) and the regenerated partition file; (2) the produced mirror std_host_text.rs (`emitted surface has no committed mirror`); (3) a transitional lib.rs (SeedMembershipUnresolved, above); (4) the partition file's own mirror gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs (`WholeCompilerRebuildRequired partition_generation_authority=[...]`); (5) lib.rs again, back to main's bytes; (6) the partition crate src/v1/stage0_std_core/src/lib.rs from `claim_executor --emit-partition-crates --write` (E0432 unresolved crate::std_host_text in the seed build). Every one is derivable from the partition row alone; heal derives none of them in one round.",
    "DEFECT 1 -- INVALID STATE: lib.rs, the stage0 crate's module list, is a seed surface the convergence planner must classify, but no row of gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_generated owns it, so the host derives UnresolvedSeedMembership for it (src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs, the `has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition` arm) and v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_first_unresolved refuses the whole stage. Any change that adds or removes a seed module changes lib.rs, so EVERY such PR refuses convergence and needs lib.rs installed by hand from the candidate tree. HARM: the heal job cannot converge a routine seed-module addition; authors install generated files outside the job that owns them.",
    "DEFECT 2 -- INVALID STATE: the host's projection of the planner outcome (required_regen_host.rs, the `convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant <value>` arm, reading regen_stage_plan_kind_label) renders RegenStagePlanningRefused as the bare word `Refused`, dropping the RegenConvergenceRefusal payload that names the refusal and its surface. HARM: a typed, located refusal reaches CI as an unlocated one; the specimen cost three remote regen runs to read a reason the model already carried. This is gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed's `every degradation is typed, located and countable` lost at the last link.",
    "DEFECT 3 -- INVALID STATE: the heal step `Refuse when the stage0 round wrote a file the seed-build writer owns` (dag/gunbc/heal_candidate_stage0.dag heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet) crashed in its own evaluation on #14317 at 7bf0694203a (2026-10-18): `error: evaluating heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet ... cause: NoSuchVariable { name: \"value\" }`. Its refusal message is built only on the drifted arm, from `map(drifted, d => d.entry.path.value as String)`, so the path it should name -- the seed-build roster file it found drifted -- never reaches CI. HARM: a typed, located refusal (`HealStage0RoundWroteSeedBuildArtifact`, naming the paths) becomes an evaluator crash with no subject; the author cannot tell which file, or whether the refusal fired at all. CEILING: structurally guaranteed (the refusal's rendering is total over its own carrier and is exercised by a control). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the overlap refusal renders every drifted path through an accessor the evaluator resolves, proved by a control that feeds a non-empty drifted population and expects the named paths in the reason.",
    "DEFECT 3 ROOT CAUSE, FOUND (2026-10-18, by bisecting #14317's 83 .dag changes on a 64 GB runner): the overlap step's crash was NOT the heal tool's -- it was THIS ROW. An earlier wording of the DEFECT 2 receipt quoted the host's format string with its placeholder in braces, and a braced identifier inside a .dag string literal is interpolation, so evaluating this module (which the overlap step's closure loads) looked up a variable named value and failed. Restoring this one file made the step exit 0; restoring any other changed file did not. The placeholder is now written with angle brackets. The step's crash therefore says nothing about heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet's own rendering, and DEFECT 3 above is withdrawn as a heal defect. What it does show is a separate hazard: a ledger row's prose can break an unrelated tool's evaluation, and the failure names the variable, not the file.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable for both -- the refusal is loud (the job fails), and a by-hand install of generator output works around defect 1; nothing mechanical prevents either. CEILING: structurally guaranteed for defect 1 (every seed surface the planner sees has an owner or a declared bootstrap role, so UnresolvedSeedMembership is unreachable for lib.rs) and for defect 2 (the planner's refusal crosses to the host as a typed value that the host renders whole).",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, AS CAPABILITIES. Defect 1: the convergence planner classifies the stage0 crate's lib.rs (and any other crate-root surface the emitter writes) with a declared role and seed membership, so a PR that adds a seed module converges in heal with no hand-installed file -- proved by a fixture that adds one module and expects a planned stage, not a refusal. Defect 2: the host renders a RegenStagePlanningRefused outcome with its full RegenConvergenceRefusal payload (variant, reason, surface), proved by a control that feeds the projection a refusal and expects the payload in the printed reason. Routed by tidy-ant-251 to Manager 2."
    "DEFECT 1, MECHANISM LOCATED AND CLOSED (2026-11-11, PR #16310, head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f): the row named the symptom (lib.rs refused twice on two states) without the link. One rule has two readers, and both asked the copy of the partition compiled into the running seed while the same emission renders that partition's mirror off the corpus on disk. (a) required_regen_host `convergence_surface_roles` built `seed_embedded_basenames` from `assembled_seed_modules(committed lib.rs mod list, generated_partition_crate_rows() compiled in)` (:7495-:7506) and `convergence_plan_from_model` (:7613) classified each changed surface against that set and built the refusal value at :7744, so a module the change ADDS to a partition crate is absent from the membership set by construction -- the row is what the PR authors -- and its own mirror classified `<basename> has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition`, which is the arm `v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction` `regen_first_unresolved` refuses the whole stage on. (b) `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `lib_rs_module_is_partition_owned` asked the same compiled copy, so the emitted lib.rs declared a mod the partition had just claimed and the next generation deleted it. Both now read one population per round: `emitted_tree_packages` reads the declared rows off the corpus (the route that already exists for the emitted-edge admission, whose own comment states why -- the rows compiled into THIS binary are the predecessor's, #12171's bootstrap deadlock broken on #12185 only by hand-seeding the mirror) and the render receives them as an argument along compile_sources_selected -> emit_resolved_for_target_selected -> emit_from_artifact_plan -> emit_artifact -> emit_rust_selected -> emit_lib_rs_from_paths -> lib_rs_module_is_partition_owned. THE FAMILY IS EIGHT CRATE ROOTS, ALL INSPECTED: the stage0 crate root (90 pub mod lines plus one plain mod compiler_tests, 91 declarations) plus the seven partition roots (stage0_runtime 1, stage0_std_core 55, stage0_std_surface 4, stage0_extdeps_languages 14, stage0_v1_artifact 2, stage0_v1_infer 23, stage0_emit_core 13 pub mod lines -- measured at this head, and the population declares exactly seven GeneratedPartitionCrateRow instances, one per root), one of which (stage0_v1_infer) is entirely #[path into ../../stage0/src re-exports of host-shell modules, the same membership question in a second syntax. Inspected and EXCLUDED, each for a reason: GeneratedFacadeCrate is a declared kind no row uses today, so there is no ninth root; gunbc_stage0_stage0_executable_assembly_generated.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs and emitted_population.rs carry zero pub mod lines (data surfaces, not roots); v1_rt.rs is one generated module whose only mod items are three inline *_tests blocks. The seven partition roots never flipped -- the candidate side already rendered them over the fresh rows, required_regen_host partition_move_explained_by_this_change calling partition_crate_boundary_emit_outcome_over(packages.rows) -- which is why only the stage0 root oscillated. The DIRECTION of that oscillation fixes the fixed point: emit_lib_rs_from_paths (v1.compiler.emit_rust, the has_compiler_tests branch) declares on the MIXED-AUTHORITY host-shell root ONLY the names no partition row owns -- the carrier words it as THE HOST SHELL DECLARES WHAT THE PARTITION DOES NOT OWN, and the subtraction is what makes the duplicate unwritable -- while wholly-generated partition roots subtract nothing. The specimen's module is owned by the v1-stage0-v1-infer row (src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag, stage0_v1_infer_modules; its crate root went 23 to 24 pub mod lines at the specimen's generation-0 install, and generated_host_shell_partition_dependencies is exactly the single package v1-stage0-v1-infer, dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_executable_assembly_generated.dag:11, which is the only package the host shell glob-re-exports), so the host shell has exactly ONE correct rendering of that root: do NOT declare the module, 90 declarations, main's bytes. It is the STALE copy that cannot subtract and so writes the module into the host shell AND into the partition crate -- one file, two compilation stories, the duplicate the carrier comment exists to prevent. The clause this row once read as the defect, lib.rs flips back to main's bytes, is therefore the surface ARRIVING at its fixed point while a predecessor population pulls it toward the duplicate; with one authority for both readers, git status over a run reports lib.rs unchanged. That same seam is where a partition crate root is written (v1_compiler_stage0_crates :915, :1080, :1125, :1206 build the path as spec.crate_dir + /src/lib.rs) and the convergence host projects and installs it itself (--emit-partition-crates at required_regen_host :6445, --emit-partition-crates --write at :6503), so the row's sixth hand-install is not a human step. THE OVERLAP GATE DOES NOT BLOCK THIS DERIVATION EITHER: the seed-build writer's roster (dag/gunbc/seed_build_artifact_emit.dag:47-62) lists Stage0CratePartitionGeneratedDagArtifact, the .dag projection, and has no .rs counterpart -- so heal's round writing src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs is not two writers for one file, and the gate stage0_round_overlap_cause / HealStage0RoundWroteSeedBuildArtifact (dag/gunbc/heal_candidate_stage0.dag:44-70, run after the round and before the writer) stays silent for it. That gate's own rule is that identical bytes are no change, which is what makes it correct that a PR adding a partition row also commits the regenerated .dag projection: that file is the writer's, and matching it byte for byte is the requirement, not staying out of it. SCOPE OF THE RESTORED CAPABILITY, stated narrowly because one of the six is not heal's to take: of the six installs the #14317 specimen listed, heal now derives the transitional lib.rs, the partition file mirror, the second lib.rs and the partition crate lib.rs; the partition row is authored by design and its .dag projection belongs to the seed-build writer above. The module's FIRST mirror stays an authorial install, and correctly so: the host refuses emitted-but-uncommitted surfaces because an author introducing a module and an emitter inventing a surface produce the identical population, and no arm computed from the populations distinguishes them -- admitting the first would be the conflation the other way. So the capability this row claims is four of the six derived with the partition row as the only authored input, plus one mirror that is committed once, under grant, by the author who introduced the module. Readers left compiled-in, with the reason: v1_compiler_stage0_crates stage0_crate_plan_outcome / stage0_crate_boundary_emit_outcome (the BUILT SEED projecting its own --emit-partition-crates boundary must answer from the seed it was built as), partition_crate_boundary_host partition_package_names (names packages for a cargo compile scope, an input to a build and not a fixed-point authority), and required_regen_host's #[test] an_emit_that_refuses_hands_back_no_files, whose emit carries no partition in flight so the assertion is the all-or-nothing file rule, which no population can change.",
    "DEFECT 1, RUNG EVIDENCE (2026-11-11, srv1, operator-run): RED, heal route -- the heal invocation (`claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope --source-root dag --source-root src/v2`) at PR #16251 head ba126e56719cf973081b48ef9401ce94acbed90a, base mirror 84f93b33ea843fe1a843b6183b05882fc0314403, identity tree:sha1:120b520230d261e99de8f368abef0cf986cd7e57, uncapped, log srv1:/tmp/red16251.log, lib.rs sampler srv1:/tmp/libsamp.out: EXIT=1 after 1h42m (09:07:06Z to 10:48:57Z). Generation 0 completed -- round.built_seed_regen 25 min, elapsed_ms=1542046, first_generation_equal=false, planned=176 executed=176 adjudicated=176 declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), FAIL generated surface drift = emitted_population.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs, lib.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs; the candidate lib.rs at 09:51:16Z was dcbb5b3ffcee863296a39cf7db1f86c1d83cd46cfabf19bc81d22fb2373f8abd with 91 pub mod lines and v1_compiler_rest_cause_text present; round.install put it on both crate roots (stage0 lib.rs to dcbb5b3f..., and src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs 24034b7e... to b8483dc29208091825d87d79f539979752942f96911be6ad30fcd7e6d634f872, 23 to 24 pub mod, the re-export root gaining the same module); round.rebuild_from_installed 7 min. NO UnresolvedSeedMembership refusal appeared on this route: generation 1 was refused AT ITS BEGIN by the one-resident-generation bound (`generation begin Refused: GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator ordinal=1 orchestrator_resident_bytes_at_first_generation=234332160 orchestrator_resident_bytes_now=5248946176 growth_bound_bytes=3221225472`), and the checkpoint then restored lib.rs to 6605bb7945fa6d1a67c4c7b2ca2659c2f6fe1e99fc6a13beff25f864b0f3f164 -- a restore, not an emitted flip. RED, author route, where the flip this defect describes is what the emission itself shows: at the same head `--required-regen` round 1 drifted lib.rs ALONE and its candidate was 6605bb7945fa6d1a67c4c7b2ca2659c2f6fe1e99fc6a13beff25f864b0f3f164, byte-identical to the base mirror, dropping `pub mod v1_compiler_rest_cause_text`. The two values are the oscillation; the 90-line one is the rendering the partition declares correct, and the build failure below is the PARTIAL install named in clause (3), not that value; round 2 seed build then failed with one E0432 and four E0433 naming that module in v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs (at :67 and :43062 of the round-0 INSTALLED emit_rust, which is not the committed file at ba126e56 -- the committed mirror carries zero occurrences). GREEN, three clauses, all required by the row. (1) AUTHOR ROUTE, fixed point, at #16310 head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f: the regenerator built from that tree's own hosts, `--required-regen --source-root dag --source-root src/v2`, iterated two rounds (round 1 drifted exactly v1_compiler_compile.rs, rc=1, elapsed_ms=1572855; that file was installed and the regenerator was rebuilt from the installed tree for round 2) and ended zero drift -- first_generation_equal=true, planned=executed=adjudicated=175, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), rc=0 -- with the change set's generated files installed: v1_compiler_compile.rs 2782274f2ac0f075d6b0e3502b74c3a4b2319b8a6a94f0e8971b36cce443af6e (blob e3b72f059523bed109cf8f0cb0375df3a4158f45), the only file that moves at that head, and v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 4dd771251c8bcb0f4316dba42a7c2cc5c2b27f65d9048d4d95d59d983903e8ee (blob ad2c0b6f6e0a11b44c5ec34474fae41c241a27a7), which drifted in NO round because its candidate was byte-identical to the committed copy. compiler_tests.rs and v1_compiler_compiler_tests_rust.rs are not in the changed set at all at that head: both are main's bytes, and the first emission moved NEITHER of them. (2) HEAL ROUTE on a scratch merge of #16251 with #16310 head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f (srv1 unit acc16251, merge 799a08c199c8ecd6ac3667e4a2bdf69fbb122116 = ba126e56 + c16948d3 by --no-ff, tree db867b6037b9e8ed5aaa572a04ae96c2b42c3cbe, HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT 4b67f390b0225e5f0d5868f83fdcaf33605dca4f, identity tree:sha1:db867b6037b9e8ed5aaa572a04ae96c2b42c3cbe, MemoryMax 64G swap 0, --regen-affected-scope kept, target/stage0-regen-candidate REMOVED and verified absent at 13:47:11Z so no candidate byte can be inherited -- every one of the 255 candidate files at the end carried mtime 14:40, written by this run). Invocation 13:55:29Z-15:42:37Z, EXIT=1, and the exit is attributable entirely to the separately named condition below. Round 1: base mirror paths=302, paths_rewritten=4, head_added_paths_kept=1, head_deleted_paths=0. GENERATION 0, the arm this row exists for: UnresolvedSeedMembership and 'has no owner' occurrences across the WHOLE invocation = 0, where the specimen produced the refusal that made regen_first_unresolved refuse the stage. round.built_seed_regen 26 min: elapsed_ms=1588592, planned=executed=adjudicated=176, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs); the drift set was EXACTLY the four membership surfaces -- emitted_population.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs, lib.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs -- and NOT v1_compiler_compile.rs (the mirror this PR installs, blob e3b72f05..., held against the base-mirror seed) and NOT compiler_tests.rs. round.install wrote them back together with the partition crate root: from the sampler at mtime 15:34:54Z, src/v1/stage0/src/lib.rs became dcbb5b3ffcee... at 91 pub mod lines WITH the module declared, and src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs became b8483dc29208... at 24 pub mod lines with the module declared -- the same bytes runB4 produced and the same bytes the specimen's round.install produced -- and round.rebuild_from_installed then COMPILED that tree. Read this plainly rather than favourably: generation 0 is the PREDECESSOR'S render, because round.built_seed_regen builds its seed crate from the base mirror (302 paths, required_regen_host.rs among them), so both roots declaring one module is what a host shell without the render-side fix emits, and it is the duplicate the carrier comment forbids -- it is not what this row calls converged. GENERATION 1 NEVER RAN, and that is the separately named condition, not this defect: 'required-regen: generation 1 begins; orchestrator resident=5248507904 (at generation 0: 236228608)' then 'regen-round-cost: refused: next generation refused; checkpoint restored: generation begin Refused: GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator ordinal=1 orchestrator_resident_bytes_at_first_generation=236228608 orchestrator_resident_bytes_now=5248507904 growth_bound_bytes=3221225472' (parent.generation_begin_admission ordinal=1 memory.current=6715666432, peak 22248300544). It is the one-resident-generation orchestrator bound, carried as a sighting on gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_resident_cost_taken_before_the_baseline_of_its_own_growth_check, and it refused the specimen at the same ordinal with the same shape. The checkpoint restore at 15:42:23Z returned src/v1/stage0/src/lib.rs to 6605bb7945fa... at 90 and the infer root to 24034b7e... at 23, after which git status --porcelain and git diff --stat were EMPTY -- an EMPTY tree there is the RESTORE, not a fixed point, and this row does not count it as one. The fixed point with the fix in force is measured by clause (3) instead, where the regenerator IS the installed tree. No generated file was hand-installed beyond the module's own first mirror, which cool-tern-790 committed under grants msg_23e9c13d and msg_0586b869, and there was no push to #16251. (3) AUTHOR ROUTE OVER THE MERGED TREE, the control that separates the two readers (srv1 unit greenb-16251, merge 729b781f923871cdffcb9bf5545474454629986f, tree 85a7c72fa749e544f13bc158a09a68addd51a87b, base mirror 4b67f390b0225e5f0d5868f83fdcaf33605dca4f, regenerator built from the merged tree's own hosts, generation 0 elapsed_ms=1580216, planned=executed=adjudicated=176, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), SeedMembership count 0): the emission MOVED THE PARTITION and the renderer together -- emitted_population.rs 78db2eb1... to 423b93bc... (the source line for the module added), gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs 8e5d6966... to 41586473... (the v1-stage0-v1-infer row's modules vector gaining it, 23 to 24) and v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 4dd77125... to 47d4a92e... (references to it 0 to 2) -- while lib.rs was NOT in the drift set: its fresh candidate, written 12:57:27Z, was 6605bb7945fa6d1a67c4c7b2ca2659c2f6fe1e99fc6a13beff25f864b0f3f164 with 90 pub mod lines and the module ABSENT, the partition-owned rendering this row now names as the fixed point. THE FOURTH SURFACE IS OWNED BY A DECLARED ROUTE, AND MEASUREMENT SEPARATES IT FROM A HAND-INSTALL: `claim_executor --emit-partition-crates` renders from the COMPILED-IN rows on purpose -- partition_crate_boundary_host.rs, run_partition_crate_boundary doc comment: 'On a round that moves the partition the compiled-in rows are the predecessor's, so the regen round renders from the candidate tree's rows (partition_crate_boundary_emit_outcome_over) and hands the outcome here' -- and heal's install uses the RENDERED-POPULATION entry, required_regen_host.rs:5975-5978 taking rows from emitted_tree_packages(workspace) and :6426 writing them with run_partition_crate_boundary_over(write=true). Measured pair on srv1 (unit runB4-16251): with the partition mirror, emitted_population.rs and v1_compiler_compile.rs installed and the binary rebuilt from that tree, --emit-partition-crates --write took src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs 24034b7e with 23 pub mod lines to b8483dc2 with 24, the same bytes heal's own install route wrote in the specimen's round.install and installing the candidate emit_rust then built clean, BUILD_B_RC=0; the same CLI on the PRE-FIX binary reported rendered=14 written=0 and the build kept exactly one E0432 at v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs:67 and four E0433 inside :43351, all naming v1_compiler_rest_cause_text in the crate root -- the identical five errors cool-tern-790 met at round 2, which is why this row calls that round a PARTIAL install of three of the six rather than a codegen defect. THE FIXED POINT ITSELF, MEASURED (srv1 unit runB5, staged control, not the acceptance run): with those five surfaces installed -- emitted_population.rs 423b93bc, the partition mirror 41586473, v1_compiler_compile.rs blob e3b72f05, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 47d4a92e, src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs b8483dc2 at 24 pub mod -- over the merged tree, and the regenerator being the build of exactly that tree, `--required-regen` returned rc=0, elapsed_ms=1426979, first_generation_equal=true, planned=executed=adjudicated=176, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), candidate-vs-tree diff list EMPTY, all 255 candidate files written by that run (13:55Z), target/stage0-regen-candidate removed beforehand at 13:40:10Z. The candidate host-shell lib.rs was 6605bb7945fa... at 90 pub mod lines with the module NOT declared, and a read-only `--emit-partition-crates` with the same binary reported rendered=14 written=0 divergent=[] -- so the infer crate root is at its own fixed point too. NO SIXTH SURFACE APPEARED. That is the statement this row needed: with the partition row authored, the six surfaces that used to be hand-installed form a closed set that the regenerator reproduces byte for byte, and the stage0 host shell settles WITHOUT declaring the module. CI on the PR: at head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f both lanes are SUCCESS -- v2-bootstrap (job 130560719439, whose step 28 'Typecheck the v1 unit-test population' was the single E0061 that the superseded mirror state produced) and heal-generated-artifacts (job 130560877728, which passed step 7 'Converge the stage0 mirrors to the seed's own fixed point' and the step 8 overlap gate). This ledger row is a .dag text edit only: it adds no carrier and no host, so it moves no generated surface, and the lanes re-run at the head that carries it.",
